│ After reviewing the code and the search results, the following key │
│ points emerge:                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    1. Bug Location and Context                     │
│                                                                    │
│ Bug Location 1:                                                    │
│ File: models.py                                                    │
│ Class: Item                                                        │
│ Method: save                                                       │
│ Intended Behavior:                                                 │
│ The save() method in Item should preserve the primary key (uid) as │
│ an immutable field. It should not allow the uid field to be        │
│ modified by external methods like reset() in the Derived model.    │
│                                                                    │
│ Bug Location 2:                                                    │
│ File: models.py                                                    │
│ Class: Derived                                                     │
│ Method: reset                                                      │
│ Intended Behavior:                                                 │
│ The reset() method in Derived should only modify non-primary key   │
│ fields (e.g., f) and not alter the uid field, which is the primary │
│ key and should remain immutable.                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                       2. Why the Bug Occurs                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • The uid field in Item is defined as an AutoField with           │
│    primary_key=True, making it the primary key of the model.       │
│  • The reset() method in Derived attempts to set self.uid = None   │
│    and self.f = False, which modifies the primary key.             │
│  • Django's ORM enforces that the primary key is immutable and not │
│    modified by user code. When the instance is saved, the database │
│    will **reassign the primary key                                 │
