│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                       2. Why the Bug Occurs                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • The uid field in Item is defined as an AutoField with           │
│    primary_key=True, making it the primary key of the model.       │
│  • The reset() method in Derived attempts to set self.uid = None   │
│    and self.f = False, which modifies the primary key.             │
│  • Django's ORM enforces that the primary key is immutable and not │
│    modified by user code. When the instance is saved, the database │
│    will reassign the primary key, leading to the observed          │
│    behavior.                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                  3. Intended Behavior of the Code                  │
│                                                                    │
